									<font color=white size=5><b>So where in the world are EoD?</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									It has been a few months since the last few EoD members have logged on.  We still chat inside our forums and like to follow what everyone is currently doing both in game (EQ), other games and of course real life.<BR><BR>I haven't got any new news for you all - however I never did publish our Rath Council experience back in January.<BR><BR>I am therefore going to take the unusual step of publishing the web internal Rath Council Raid publically.  Take it as you will:<BR>Maj<BR><BR><BR><BR>I logged on bang on 7pm to find a fair few guild in PoEB, PoE and in Tranquility. Janaria and Til were already in PoEB - they had camped their the night before and right away sent me a tell saying they had a CoH link ready. I was quite pleased with this as I blew the CoH link when Coher and I took a TL out the night before. I had reservations though about an attempt this night. I knew Tiny and San would be off and of course Argeye left us Fri night so we would be two clerics and an enchanter down. I was thinking we could do the rings - although boring and torturous at least we could add to our PoEB flagged count which would on future Rath attempts reduce our need to piggy in.<BR><BR>The members started to pile into Earth and lots were already logging back in PoEB. Before long I was suprised to find we had a 50 man raid. Enchanter/Bard wise was looking good too - No San but we had Chant, Clib, Halk, Sev, Bard and Eg - 6 capable people and 6 experienced people. We had Rez, Saint, Cel for clerics at first - way short of the number needed for Rath - however they would form the core MT crew. I asked the raid if anyone knew any clerics that would like to come along for flags. Clib and Ciniel produced the goods. We got three guest clerics. Later we also had Saveyor login and another guest - Shadowcaster. We had a decent amount of druids, shaman and paladins too. It's funny because I always start to write that we had a certain class present and then I think of another that's just as needed. Usually on raids you need clerics and DPS. In PoP however the needed classes varies considerably. In the beginning yes you need clerics and dps - in releases like Kunark, Velios etc. PoP Gods forced you to use various strategies and therefore made you use other classes. The Rath is like a collection of many events and forces you to stock up. This is a nice factor for ALL people being involved - but its a mother to resource.<BR><BR>All of a sudden it seemed like we had a Rath raid force. We had 65 in the raid (with more to follow later) and the right quantity of the right classes. Jan, Coher and Gabob began to CoH everyone over. It did take around 2 hours before we started to pull the mobs. I know this is a long time and I know despite what I say you'll still get impatient - but I'll say it anyway. Getting the right number of people in the raid window, piggying in 10-15 people, CoHing them down, carefully adjusting the groups so that you can actually handle the Rath encounter takes time. Remember 70 people is a large number. The larger the number and the more sensitive the encounter the longer it takes. If you want to kill Vindi in Kael with 10 people grouping takes 1-2 minutes - that's at the bottom of the scale - you can work up from there..<BR><BR>We have all learnt a fair bit from our attempts over the past two weeks. Indeed we only entered PoEB on 5th of January. Since that time we learnt what it takes to mez and tank the mobs. That sounds easy - and indeed many people post on various boards as such. But the detail that lies underneath is much harder. For example, the mezzable mobs don't play by the rules. I understand from Sony's website that it is a bug - which has been around for 8+ months - so mezzing becomes 'unstable'. Mix unstable mezzing with mobs which hit for quad 3k - i.e. 12k in a round then a break becomes a dead enchanter. Of course it is not only down to the enchanter. With 70 people on a raid the chances of someone hitting, dotting, AEing, nuking or otherwise breaking your mez becomes very high. Some people don't read the raid chat. Some people don't listen (read) when you tell them that these mobs if woke will wipe your raid. So 'mezzing a few mobs' isn't as easy as it may sound. Indeed if you had to mez one of these for 10 minutes - I guess it would be ok - but imagine mezzing these guys for 2 hours?? 2 hours isn't funny - that's probably the minimum for most guilds that have not already entered Time to do it in. Imagine doing it for 5 hours ? Well - enough of mezzing..lets talk for a moment about tanking. These mobs quad for 3k. Every 10% they drop in DPS output until around 0% they end up hitting for 800 quad. 800 Quad on a mostly slowable mob is still a possible max of 3200 non def. If you get an average EP tank - which we have quite a few of - most decent geared for our guild status then every 5 seconds that's a respectable amount to heal. In addition to that, they have to maintain agro, not kill it, not riposte on it and maintain its position - for possibly up to 2 hours depending on how the other '66' people are doing.. Of course, not all clerics, druids and even both + shaman can keep this going. Some clerics can ch solo on a tank. Some shaman can keep a tank going with a druid. But not all clerics, druids, shaman and tanks can make it work perfectly. Indeed I know now which tanks and clerics can do it - but for the Rath you need 5 groups capable of keeping the tanking going for as long as you need - that's 5 perfect combinations. This is the problem with the Rath - or the challenge - and that is the test of your resources.<BR><BR>I think given the absolute perfect classes then I agree 56 people is the minimum you could do this with - if they are not already Time/GoD/OOW armoured. They'd have to have a lot of EP gear though and VT stuff - i.e. what the PoP winners would have had - certainly comparable to what we have now. But the reality is and our guild is no different - you will not have 56 perfectly geared/aa people for this event - you will have shortfalls. The trick is - and one of the reasons why it takes so long to group people up is making sure you put the right guys together.<BR><BR>Well we finished the grouping around 915pm. We began to pull the mezzable mobs. Experienced has 'painfully' taught us to split the mobs up. So the plan tonight was to do just that. We got six locked down - all the mezzable mobs. We then moved the raid out to begin on the offtankable mobs. While we were dealing with the first offtankable mob Egfrith got chain resists and his mez broke. He died, then his mob killed Chanti. We then had two mobs on the run. Sev died too. Make that three mobs.. We killed one off but two went back to the spawn point. We ressed up and we had to wait until they regened.<BR><BR>This at least proved one thing - and that was splitting them up although was more complicated regarding space would at least half our recovery time. By now it was getting on for 11pm. We got the three mezzed mobs locked down again. Eg went LD after he died so Chanti took his mob as well as her own. We had Kamven permanently with her so mana wasn't an issue.<BR><BR>We locked the 7th mob down and Zavia tanked this one. We got to work on the 8th mob - for Tweefiny. Unfortunately Sev got banished and didn't make it back in time. His mob killed him and quite a few others before we axed it. The problem appears to be that the banish agro radius is probably five times the agro radius of a mob. This means that nearly anywhere in the Rath area a mob could banish anyone with any kind of agro list. It doesn't even have to be someone on the top of the agro list - although this is more likely at the start. Halfway through whacking a mob however an enchanter/bard actively mezzing is very likely to get banished to some random position. It happened to Chanti also but she made it back in time before her mezzes broke.<BR><BR>Maybe it was actually a blessing in disguise that Sev lost his mob as we had no one to do C or haste. We decided to continue collecting the offtank mobs. We had a few issues with mob 9. Ruth accidentally killed his mob on riposts. We got him another and his group started to deal with it. We collected 10 and 11 - this time the paladins Ciniel and Karadim getting some action. Unfortunately a cleric (we think a guest although don't really know) put a MoK or other reverse DS on a mob. This did 34 damage a strike and eventually Ruth's mob died. I was quite pissed by this time and chaos at mob 9 when we were up to 11 was the last thing we needed. Ruth and I had some tells and I came down on Ruth. Ruth gated and logged out. It wasn't Ruth's fault - as it was clearing a cleric that had cast it - I was mostly angry because I didn't know this DS was on the mob. We beat down a new mob 9 and Reborrn took over.<BR><BR>We repulled mob 6 - Sev's mezzable mob. We beat it down but we were out of patchers - only the core MT clerics, two paladins and I remained that could cast a heal. At 29% of the mobs life Drigar died. The mob - even though slowed beat up and killed quite a few people - of course we were out of def tanks (wars) and the SKs that took over were getting one rounded (don't forget the mezzable mobs don't decrease their output dmg even at 0%). Luckily Eg got it mezzed. We ressed in Drigar, rebuffed him and waited for his def. Trying to handle a 12k per round mob with 16 people is very tough - well it is exactly like doing Magma in PoF with the same number - HARD - but doable. During this time the group at mob 9 again had issues. Reborrn bit the bullet and his group got killed. Celsus quickly got on the mob and a few of the transient raid came over to help out while we got them ressed. While we were dealing with this - group 7-8 and 10 were having mana issues. We had necros running all over the place feeding. I thought at this stage we were going to wipe just through pure lack of mana. It seems like a few people were doing tasks they should not have been and some were not doing tasks they should have been. It is so very very important on the Rath that every does a single easy repeated task over and over and over again. Remember we are all cogs in a mechanical giant. The cogs must be in time and doing what they do - nothing more and nothing less. If people start to do more than they should they go oom. If people do less than they should others around them go oom. For example, a cleric CH the tank - that is it. A druid or paladin cure the group - that's it. A shaman perma Q and slow - that's it. I think some people were healing and curing. Curers not curing but healing - badly. clerics trying to heal and cure etc. Rath has no space for slackers. Indeed if there were slackers - and there were - I find out pretty fast when their group can't handle it.<BR><BR>We got the groups back on their feet and continued to mack mob 6 - Sev's mob back to 0%. He mezzed it and we debuffed the final mob. The tension was mounting. Bardeta's equivalent of 'Are we there yet?' was happening so much it looked like background wallpaper in my window. Drig's def was down. I was going to call for us to engage but Drig persuaded me not to. I guess we could wait another 3 minutes. After all taking a 12k per round mob with no def and only 4 healers is pretty suicidal. We waited... 11 mobs on 0%-3%. One mob left. We waited. We just had to kill this last mob and we could finish the rest. We also knew that a mez could break any second - kill an enchanter and cause a catastrophic domino affect that would wipe us in our brightest hour. We waited.<BR><BR>Def was up. We pulled, rooted, I got banished and Drigar engaged. It was perfect. We smacked it down then on 29% I made the call to kill the mobs. This may sound like an easy order to give but to be honest 29% can still take 1-2 minutes. If you call the order and then suddenly Drigar dies you probably wont be able to kill the last mob - and by then your offtanks would have killed their mob - given that their clerics/druids in group just have to cast 1-2 nukes to finish it. So give the order too soon and you may blow it- give it too late and you may run out of time. Remember you have 7 minutes from the first death. It should be enough...but..there is always a chance for a mess up and with mobs that pump out high dps you can loose an entire raid in 5 seconds.<BR><BR>The offtanks killed their mobs in moments - about a minute later mob 12 was dead and we moved to Sev's mezzed mob just outside the centre. We nuked it - Sev died - expected - we moved to Chantis, engaged - Chant died - again expected, we killed the second mob beside Chant. We then rushed over to the cave. We had used 3 minutes - 4 minutes remain. We only had 3 mobs left to kill. Drigar could spend a few moments taunting while we reslowed them.<BR><BR>3...2......1<BR><BR>The final mob, BANG...3 minutes left and the Avatar of Earth pops immediately on the last Council members death!!<BR><BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:37 2005] Rezella tells the raid, 'fuck yes !'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:39 2005] Severos tells the group, 'we did it?'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:41 2005] Ninadin tells the raid, 'YES YES YES'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:42 2005] The healing chorus fades away.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:44 2005] You tell your raid, 'stay in cave'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:45 2005] Severos tells the group, 'WEEEE'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:45 2005] Maryam tells the raid, '=)'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:46 2005] Karadim tells the guild, 'grr back'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:48 2005] Ericpuzzle tells the raid, 'we have not won yet'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:48 2005] Swiftee tells the raid, 'yes I got kill shot'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:49 2005] Ciniel tells the raid, 'can you feel that HUNNEY ! !!!!'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:52 2005] Tweefiny tells the raid, 'HE IS THERE WOOT !!'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:53 2005] You tell your raid, 'Avatar of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:54 2005] You shout, 'Avatar of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:56 2005] Spiritbane tells the raid, 'we not done yet guys...stay calm..'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:57 2005] You say to your guild, 'Avatar of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:50:57 2005] Severos tells the raid, 'btw, could need a rezz'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:00 2005] Halkios tells the raid, 'need cure and heal pls asap !'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:00 2005] Sjefen tells the raid, 'click while you can'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:01 2005] Ninadin tells the guild, 'we did it )'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:01 2005] Your spell did not take hold.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:05 2005] Garoid tells the raid, 'LISTEN UP !!!'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:06 2005] Glhamdring tells the guild, 'brrriiiiinnnggggg'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:07 2005] Rezella tells the raid, 'rez the deads'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:11 2005] Katter tells you, 'want me to log danaeb back in?'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:12 2005] You tell your raid, 'res up'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:12 2005] Muva tells the raid, 'Click me'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:17 2005] Chimerik tells the raid, 'rez inc Muva'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:21 2005] You told dreamss, 'come kite'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:23 2005] Caflor tells you, 'can Dana log back in ?'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:25 2005] draemss is not online at this time.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:26 2005] Ninadin tells the guild, 'Kara in Cave'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:27 2005] Bastyx tells you, 'gratz :P'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:28 2005] Abedina tells the raid, 'Rezzing Bardeta'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:30 2005] Dreamss tells you, 'round centre?'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:31 2005] You told dreamss, 'lets play slow the mob'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:33 2005] Bastyx tells you, 'the hard part done :p'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 01:51:34 2005] You told Dreamss, 'aye'<BR><BR><BR>People had said in guides and forums that AoE would charge the raid. He did no such thing. His agro is very high however - although he didn't do anything until I poked my nose up onto the central area. He charged me and I casted a slow. He then proceeded to chase me around the centre. We ressed up and rebuffed. Dreamss got it slowed and continued to kite while I organised the raid.<BR><BR>Avatar of Earth hits for 2500 quad. He has an ae which causes a 95% mem blur, dot and causes spells to cost double. It had a -350 MR check - which as we know you can't rely on resisting - in fact it generally is unresistable (at 525 MR).<BR><BR>Dreamms pulled it in and Drigar engaged. We had a few deaths - myself included (thanks to memblur) but only 5-6 out of the full raid. He died fairly easily. He is documented as being just as easy as a council member and if you get that far you 'shouldn't' have a problem. Of course with all the council men dead we had a full 72 people smoking his ass.<BR><BR>THE AVATAR OF EARTH WAS SLAIN!!!!!<BR><BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:55 2005] Pollett says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:55 2005] Celsus is surrounded by an aura of mystical energy.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:55 2005] You tell your raid, 'res deads'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:56 2005] Ninadin tells the raid, 'woot'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:56 2005] Radgey's voice booms.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:56 2005] Radgey's song ends.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:56 2005]<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:57 2005] Chimerik begins to cast a spell.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:57 2005] Reborrn tells the raid, 'WOOOOOTAGE, OWNED'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:57 2005] Clibikie says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:58 2005] You tell your raid, 'all hail Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:58 2005] Pinedilea tells the raid, 'GRATS )'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:58 2005] Bastyx tells the raid, 'gratz !!'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:58 2005] Garoid begins to cast a spell.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:58 2005] Grogo tells the raid, 'WOOOOOOOOOT WEEEEE LEEEZ SHIZZZ'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:06:59 2005] Severos tells the raid, 'WOOOOT'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:00 2005]<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:00 2005] Glhamdring says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:00 2005] Cruss begins to cast a spell.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:00 2005] Vassil says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:00 2005] Pollett says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:01 2005] You say, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:01 2005] Sainted says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:01 2005] Shadowcaster tells the raid, 'Grats EoD :)'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:02 2005] Rezella says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:04 2005] Dreamss tells the raid, 'woot grats :)'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:06 2005] The ground begins to shake and crack at your feet. The quakes are powerful but you are not haltered by them. Suddenly a formation of earth begins to coalesce in your hand.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:11 2005] Vassil tells the raid, 'FUCK YEAH'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:13 2005] Bardeta tells the raid, 'WE ARE FUCKING LEET'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:15 2005] Clibikie tells the raid, 'woot - Mound of Living Stone'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:24 2005] Impnus says out of character, 'Grats you all :)'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:24 2005] Coher says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:25 2005] Extravaganza tells the raid, 'Weee =D.'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:29 2005] You tell your raid, 'who needs res?'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:31 2005] Silullei says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:31 2005] Tyco tells the raid, 'Mound of Living Stone!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:32 2005] Sjefen joined the raid.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:32 2005] Stuemper tells the raid, 'need rezz plz 8)'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:33 2005] Reborrn tells you, 'how many flags he give?'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:33 2005] Janaria tells the raid, 'me pl'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:33 2005] Sjefen says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:33 2005] Ninadin begins to cast a spell.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:34 2005] Sainted tells the guild, 'we kick so much ass =)'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:34 2005] You no longer have a target.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:34 2005] You no longer have a target.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:35 2005] Your Karana's Tear shimmers briefly.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:35 2005] You begin casting Quiescence.<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:36 2005] Bardeta tells the raid, 'meee'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:36 2005] Aanien says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:36 2005] Tyco tells the raid, 'oooh baby'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:37 2005] Janaria tells the raid, 'rezz me pl'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:38 2005] Severos says, 'Hail, Essence of Earth'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:38 2005] Spiritbane tells the guild, 'rezz the deads :)'<BR>[Sun Jan 16 02:07:41 2005] Ericpuzzle tells the raid, 'woot'<BR><BR><BR>The Essence of Earth spawned and people began to hail. We ressed in the deads. There was easily 80 flags in the Essence. In fact - I'd say it is unlimited - only by time (15 mins). We managed to get a good 8 alts/others flagged too. The Avatar dropped silk legs, leaf arms and sword. Grats to Summi, Celeni and Egfrith respectively.<BR><BR>We are now 4/5ths to Time! We just downed one of if not the hardest EP Gods there is. Some people say Coirnav is harder - but most guilds get stuck on the Rath. I will let you know after we have a pop at squidface! Fennin and Xegony are one thing - but getting the Rath down is still a very respectable milestone in EP. It separates the EP farmers from the Time progression guilds.<BR><BR>That was one hell of a mammouth raid. From 7pm-9pm doing pigg, coh and groups and from 9-2am doing the encounter. 5 hours of mezzing for some. 2 hours of offtanking for others.<BR><BR>IF everything went perfectly I'd say we could improve that time to around 4 hours total raid - and 3 hours to encounter - maybe even a little less. The time goes when you have mistakes - i.e. mob deaths, enchanter/bard deaths or having to wait for mobs to regen. If you analyse our raid we had all 3 - and some a couple of times over. If you consider that we had to do 5 mobs again - we actually locked down 17 Rath council members. That's 17 mobs - 3k quadders to 0%. We also had a lot of time due to feeding and ressing a couple of groups. We also had to wait for two mobs to regen from 0 to 100% again. If you remove that from our time - you probably find the encounter would of took 2.5 hours - not 5.<BR><BR>Still - it gives us the opportunity to improve. SHOCK? Well we will have to do Rath at least one more time! We have now 50 people flagged for the Earth part of their Time key. We will hit Fennin, Xegony and Rath at least once more each on scheduled advertised days (Fri) before we properly start to focus on Time. Coirnav we will do twice also.<BR><BR>Well - Saturday night was a massive victory - and I didn't even think we would go to PoEB that night - let alone WTF OWN IT!<BR><BR>Maj <BR>
